<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Weather</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>weather
</pre>
<p>Look at the sky: it is cloudless, cloudy, rainy, or lit by flashes of 
lightning. You must be outdoors to see it; indoors, and in some places 
under the earth or out of this world, "You can't see the sky from here."
</p><p>The weather changes by itself, and from place to place. It matters: some 
spells need the sky clear, others a storm (see <a cmd='#'>Help Clear Skies</a> and 
<a cmd='#'>Help Storm Call</a>), and night and bad weather make it darker.
</p><p><b>Weather watching</b> is a skill the sorcerers teach (from guild level 
12, up to 35%). With it, weather also gives you a forecast: whether the 
weather will probably become worse or better. Don't trust it too far: 
for now it only says "better" while lightning flashes, and "worse" at 
all other times.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Time</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Clear Skies</a>
